    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1GLOBAL__DIAG2" kindref="compound">GLOBAL_DIAG2</ref> register bit definitions (datasheet Rev 1.2 §5.3.2.7). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>TLE92466ED has <bold>no</bold> <computeroutput>OTP_ECC_WARN</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>REG_ECC_WARN</computeroutput> bits. Successful single-bit ECC correction is silent. Only uncorrectable multi-bit flips set the ERR bits.<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>REG_ECC_ERR</computeroutput> disables power stages and forces Config Mode (§4.9.7).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>OTP_ECC_ERR</computeroutput> is factory OTP content; write-1-to-clear <bold>twice</bold>. It re-asserts if the cells stay corrupt and does <bold>not</bold> by itself force Config Mode.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>OTP_VIRGIN</computeroutput> must always be 0 (1 = unprogrammed OTP address). </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
